* GPSS Program: Discrete Event Simulation and Resource Management
* This program simulates a simple system with entities arriving, being processed by a resource, and then leaving.
* It demonstrates basic GPSS constructs: GENERATE, ADVANCE, SEIZE, RELEASE, and TERMINATE.

* Define the system parameters
PARAMETER MAX_TIME=1000      * Maximum simulation time
PARAMETER ARRIVAL_INTERVAL=10 * Time between entity arrivals
PARAMETER SERVICE_TIME=5      * Time to process an entity

* Initialize the simulation
SIMULATION
  GENERATE ARRIVAL_INTERVAL      * Generate entities every ARRIVAL_INTERVAL time units
  SEIZE RESOURCE                  * Seize the resource (single server)
  ADVANCE SERVICE_TIME            * Hold the entity for SERVICE_TIME (processing)
  RELEASE RESOURCE                * Release the resource
  TERMINATE                       * Terminate the entity

END
* Note: In a real GPSS implementation, you would need to initialize the random number generator
* and set the simulation end time. This is a simplified example for demonstration purposes.
* Actual GPSS syntax may vary depending on the specific GPSS implementation being used.
